.Dd July 29, 2026
.Dt SERVICECTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm servicectl
.Nd control interface to serviced
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm status | services | reload
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm stop Ar label
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm install Ar path.cap
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm verify
.Op Fl -effective
.Op Fl -policy Ar file
.Ar path.cap ...
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm policy-check Ar file
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm deps Ar program
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm bundles
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the administrative command-line interface to
.Xr serviced 8 .
Each invocation opens a connection to the
.Xr serviced 8
control socket, sends one command, prints the result, and exits.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "check manifest"
.It Cm status
Display the overall status of
.Xr serviced 8
and a table of all loaded services.
For each service, the output includes the label, current state
.Pq running, stopped, starting, or stopping ,
PID (if running), restart policy, and restart count.
Available to any user.
.It Cm services
List all loaded services.
The output is identical to the
.Cm status
command.
Available to any user.
.It Cm reload
Reload service manifests from disk.
New manifests are loaded and their services started, changed
manifests trigger a graceful restart of the affected service,
and manifests removed from disk cause the corresponding service
to be gracefully stopped.
The dependency graph is re-validated before any changes are
applied; if the new graph would contain a cycle, the reload
is rejected and running services are unaffected.
.Pp
Requires root privileges.
.It Cm stop Ar label
Gracefully stop a running service.
Sends SIGTERM and waits for the service's configured
.Va stop_timeout
before escalating to SIGKILL.
.Pp
Requires root privileges.
.It Cm install Ar path.cap
Install a
.Pa .cap
bundle to
.Pa /Capabilities/ .
The bundle is verified before installation.
Source ownership is not preserved: the installed policy tree is created as
root so its original owner cannot modify it after verification.
After copying, run
.Cm servicectl reload
to register the new services.
.Pp
Requires root privileges.
.It Cm verify Op Fl -effective Op Fl -policy Ar file Ar path.cap ...
Validate one or more
.Pa .cap
bundles.
Checks that bundle structure and every manifest are valid, binaries exist and
are executable, provided names are unique, component interfaces resolve to
exactly one compatible provider, provider pins match, and dependencies are
acyclic.
When multiple paths are supplied, their combined provider and dependency
graph is checked.
Consumer bundles should be verified together with the provider bundles they
will be deployed with.
The summary prints each resolved component provider and every derived
dependency, including effective values for defaults omitted by manifests.
The
.Fl -effective
flag documents and makes explicit this output mode.
With
.Fl -policy ,
provider defaults and per-service overrides are loaded from
.Ar file
before resolution.
.It Cm policy-check Ar file
Validate the complete schema, types, limits, and duplicate-selection rules of
a serviced administrator policy without loading any bundles.
.It Cm deps Ar program
Inspect a dynamic executable's library dependencies and retained
.Pa .note.5bsd.components
records, then print a minimal provider-neutral component manifest fragment.
The result is advisory and must be reviewed and declared explicitly;
dependency discovery never grants authority.
.It Cm bundles
List all installed bundles from
.Pa /Capabilities/System/
and
.Pa /Capabilities/ ,
showing bundle ID, version, and service count for each.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--policy file"
.It Fl s Ar socket
Connect to the
.Xr serviced 8
control socket at
.Ar socket
instead of the default
.Pa /var/run/serviced.sock .
.It Fl -effective
Print the complete effective manifest, including omitted defaults and resolved
provider dependencies.
.It Fl -policy Ar file
Apply the specified administrator provider policy while verifying bundles.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Nm
exits 0 on success and >0 if an error occurred.
An exit status of
.Dv EX_UNAVAILABLE
(69) indicates that the control socket could not be reached,
typically because
.Xr serviced 8
is not running.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check whether
.Xr serviced 8
is running and list services:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# servicectl status
.Ed
.Pp
Reload manifests after adding a new service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# servicectl reload
.Ed
.Pp
Install and activate a bundle:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# servicectl install /path/to/MyApp.cap
# servicectl reload
.Ed
.Pp
Verify a bundle's integrity:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# servicectl verify /path/to/MyApp.cap
.Ed
.Pp
Validate administrator selection policy and show the complete effective
consumer configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# servicectl policy-check /etc/serviced/policy.ucl
# servicectl verify --policy /etc/serviced/policy.ucl \e
    /Capabilities/System/FileSystemCmp.cap /path/to/MyApp.cap
.Ed
.Pp
Suggest provider-neutral declarations from an ELF program:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ servicectl deps /path/to/MyApp.cap/bin/myapp
.Ed
.Pp
Connect to an alternate control socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# servicectl -s /tmp/test-serviced.sock status
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr serviced 5 ,
.Xr serviced 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
